The `Sprintf` function is a variadic function that formats a string and returns it as a `Str` object. It is used extensively throughout the `w3m` codebase for various purposes, including HTML generation, message formatting, and file/URL manipulation.
</description>

<requirements>

<requirement>
The `fmt` argument should be a null-terminated string. This is a fundamental requirement for any C-style string function.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The format specifiers in the `fmt` string should be valid and correspond to the types of the variadic arguments. Mismatched specifiers can lead to memory corruption or crashes.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The number of variadic arguments must match the number of format specifiers in the `fmt` string. A mismatch can lead to reading from invalid memory locations.
</requirement>
<requirement>
